  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the total number of students who wear glasses and those who don't by rounding to the nearest $10$:\n\n- wear glasses: $117⟶120$\n\n- don't wear Glasses: $361⟶360$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of students who wear glasses to those who don’t is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{120}{360}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{120÷10}{360÷10}=\\frac{12}{36}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷12}{36÷12}=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of students who wear glasses to those who don’t is approximately $1:3.$",
